# HyperMarkDown Language Specification

HyperMarkDown is a document language based on CommonMark that extends Markdown
with wikilinks, embeds, block anchors, structured frontmatter, mathematical
notation (inline and block LaTeX expressions), and visualizations (diagrams,
graphs, and charts).

Beyond static document representation, HyperMarkDown introduces the concept of
executable documents through the integration of HQL (Hyper Query Language).
Embedded HQL cells allow documents to query data, perform computations, and
incorporate their results into the document itself.

This document is the language standard for HyperMarkDown. It
defines the syntax, semantics, parsing rules, vault structure, and reference
resolution, building upon
[CommonMark 0.31.2](https://spec.commonmark.org/0.31.2/). Its purpose is to
ensure consistent interpretation of HyperMarkDown documents across independent
implementations.

!!! info "Version"
    This document specifies HyperMarkDown **0.1.0**. The version follows the
    rules under [Versioning and Authority](#versioning-and-authority), and
    what each version changed is recorded in
    [the language's changelog](https://github.com/ewiger/hypermarkdown/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md).

